### During the period from April 4, 2020, to October 4, 2020, did any bills that originated in a Republican-majority chamber of the Wisconsin Legislature receive a final passage vote?
Answer: Yes, during the specified period, at least one bill originating in the Republican-majority Wisconsin State Assembly received a final passage vote. Specifically, "Assembly Bill 1038 passed on April 14, 2020 and was quickly taken up and passed by the State Senate the following day," ultimately becoming 2019 Wisconsin Act 185.

Source URL: https://lindner-marsack.com/news/2020/04

### What was the legislative activity (e.g., number of bills introduced, committee votes, floor votes) of the Wisconsin State Legislature between April 4, 2020, and October 4, 2020?
Answer: Based on the search result, the Wisconsin State Legislature passed at least one bill during the time frame in question: **2019 Wisconsin Act 185**, known as the COVID-19 Response Bill, was "passed on April 14, 2020" by the Assembly and "was quickly taken up and passed by the State Senate the following day" (April 15, 2020). The search result does not contain sufficient information on other legislative activities such as the total number of bills introduced or detailed floor and committee votes during the six-month period.

